  "reviews": [
    {
      "game": "Call of Duty: Black Ops 7 - Vault Edition",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/20549/450x258/call-of-duty-black-ops-7-vault-edition-xbox-series-x-s-pc-xbox-one-microsoft-store-cover.jpg?v=1790283600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/20549-buy-call-of-duty-black-ops-7-vault-edition-xbox-series-x-s-pc-xbox-one-microsoft-store/",
      "user": "lloydofminecraft",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/30807463-1777577296.jpg",
      "sentiment": "dislike",
      "content": "Oh boy...\n\n\n\nWhere should I start? As someone who doesn't play many FPS games, I wasn't aware of just how terrible Black Ops 7 really was. I just checked Steam, and honestly, I wasn't at all surprised that the game had overwhelmingly negative reviews. It’s mostly down to the multiplayer, but since I only ever play the campaign anyway, that wasn't an issue for me. So, I picked up the game, and the first thing I have to vent about is that Activision still hasn't managed to enable their anti-cheat for Linux users. But that’s not really relevant to the game itself—and it’s nothing new—so I just booted into Windows and downloaded it.210 GB?! Are you serious, Activision?! 210 damn gigabytes?! Oookay, other games aren't much smaller either, so I gritted my teeth and jumped in.\n\n\n\nEight hours. EIGHT HOURS for an €80 full-price title! Should I even get started on how many bugs there are—how the multiplayer campaign aspect sounds awesome on paper, but the execution is an absolute disaster? Good grief... XD \n\n\n\nAt least the game is well-optimized. (Oooor it’s the hardware—that’s always a possibility, of course ;))\n\n\n\nSo, my verdict?\n\n\n\nCall of Duty = total crap. Anti-cheat = even bigger crap. Everyone who read this review: absolute legends.\n\n\n\nThanks for reading (assuming you didn't just skip ahead ?) and yeah.\n\n\n\nSee ya! :D"
    },
    {
      "game": "Disco Elysium - The Final Cut",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/9753/450x258/disco-elysium-the-final-cut-pc-mac-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1790283600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/9753-buy-disco-elysium-the-final-cut-pc-mac-game-steam/",
      "user": "gamer-e685b82",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "A very unique game solving a murder. You take the role of a police offer attempting to solve.\n\n\n\nEnvironment very interactive and lots of voice acting that sets a great tone. The art style is very individualised also with an expansive area to cover."
    },
    {
      "game": "Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/19517/450x258/resonance-a-plague-tale-legacy-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1790283600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/19517-buy-resonance-a-plague-tale-legacy-pc-steam/",
      "user": "Dotista",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/444812-1512725691.jpg",
      "sentiment": "dislike",
      "content": "I loved the two first installments. But this one is poor in story creativity. I deduced the whole plot at the 1/3 of the game. There is holes in the lore, a lack of explanations. The choices characters make are very doubtful. Always taken by emotion or attachment, even if thousands of ppl lives are at stake.\n\n\n\nThe gameplay is Tomb Raider like or should I say Dumb Raider. They even copied the white paintings on cliffs to attract the player to climb.\n\n\n\nFights and gameplay in general is very generic, without innovation. I insist, none. Because at minimum this game is a copy of the two first.\n\n\n\nAnd for the LAST critic but not the LEAST, go ***, go BROKE.\n\nAsobo, you chose your side about the fate of or our western civilization, I chose mine.\n\nI will never give them money again."
    },
    {
      "game": "Fae Farm",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/16459/450x258/fae-farm-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1790283600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/16459-buy-fae-farm-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "Suepixels",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/4460059-1530138549.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Actually, I don't like and even don't play many games, but Faefarm is a pretty, cute, and colorful carefully designed farming life-sim game infused with fairy magic. However, I had some major difficulties at the very beginning with how to ace the fishing skill and figuring out some other things about how they work. To me this wasn't intuitive enough (no tutorial); Jump in and learn on the fly. Unless you played any other farming simulation game, you need to figure out stuff yourself. Once you make it somehow work, it's pure joy. I love the emotes for how they show their emotions. Conversion with the townies is cute and sometimes even humorous. Yet, there is no depth and they are limited, as once you play, though, they get repetitive. The soundtrack is beyond beautiful and I love how adorable this game looks. I love to explore all corners in this world. The designs and characters are cute; there is not much to select from at the beginning, but you can unlock clothes, hairstyles, and craft dyes; build your home and have multiple homes; decorate them; have magic seasonal and magical crops; and have a couple of other things. Once you are able to do spells, you can craft magic items and wings. I'm six hours in and enjoy it now—so much so when I dive into faefarm, I forget the world around me. Just started to build friendships and relationships. NPCs have a charming character attached to them. The World, the characters, and the music are absolutely beautiful. Buy it on sale here and enjoy it. I'm not sure if I would pay for the DLCs at full price but on sale I would try them. Would love to see a continuation or a sequel but I read Phoenix Labs belongs now to Gambit—I hope there is still a future and I do adore and love the artstyle and gameplay. It could use a bit more depth but that besides - it was 100% worth it for me."
    }
  ],
